Anyway, Jack, you're 75 and I'm 73.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:34.730
I've known you all my life.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:44.700
I've known you all my life, Jack, and I can truly say this, I've never met a nicer man.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:49.760
You're a fine man, and I only hope when I get to be your age, I'll look as good as Groucho does, too.

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:21.280
Ladies and gentlemen, it's time to hear from the man himself, who is respected, admired, and loved by his fellow professionals, and from everyone who knows him, I guess that would be most of the world, Mr. Jack Benny.

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:58.870
In reviewing the evening, I would like to say, first of all, how very flattered I am that the vice president could be here tonight, even for this short time.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.410
I'd like to say that even though Mr. Agnew and I have been friends for a long time,

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:14.450
he knows that at the last election, I did not vote Republican.

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:18.530
Neither did I vote Democratic.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.020
You see, I happen to be a registered Whig.

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:33.590
And once I join a party, brother, I stick with it.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.860
I'd like to say a few words about our Toastmaster, Johnny Carson.

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:54.500
One of his gags was the fact that I have to take a Dramamine when I make love.

00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:59.960
And Johnny, in answer to that, I can only say...

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:02.640
I never take a Dramamine.

00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:06.140
I take a Dexedrine to keep me awake.

00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:18.920
Then he mentioned the fact, as did some others, about my walk.

00:24:19.360 --> 00:24:23.980
Now, all the comedians, they claim I walk very effeminately.

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:25.990
I walk like a girl.

00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:29.980
Well, in fact, my very dear friend.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:41.620
Phil Harris once said about me when we were together. He was walking behind me. He said one

00:24:41.620 --> 00:24:47.040
of the funniest things I've ever heard. He said, you know what? You could put a dress on Benny

00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:57.600
and take him anywhere. Well, maybe I do. I don't think anybody can help the way he walks.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:24:59.880
Maybe I walk like a girl.

00:25:00.160 --> 00:25:03.240
But believe me, I am not effeminate.

00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:06.680
Have I bothered any of you fellows?

00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:19.440
We go to Dennis Day, who has been with me for many, many years.

00:25:19.870 --> 00:25:26.550
I had him tell him the facts of life and all about the birds and the bees and everything.

00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:29.030
And now he's married and he has 10 or 11 children.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.840
Evidently, I made it very interesting.

00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:44.600
Of course, it was the great Will Rogers who once said, I never met a man I didn't like.

00:25:45.820 --> 00:25:48.220
Obviously, he never met Milton Berle.

00:25:53.220 --> 00:25:55.300
Anyway, Milton, thanks for being here.

00:25:56.720 --> 00:25:59.980
Whether your speech was original or not, it's the fault.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:12.520
that counts. Now I've taken a lot of good ribbing tonight and I liked it and I'm sure it was all in

00:26:12.520 --> 00:26:18.800
good fun as all of these Friars affairs are. I've only got one complaint which I marked down there

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:28.300
that how could Ed Sullivan accuse me of stealing his personality. I know we both work alike but

00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:29.960
when I smile

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:42.490
it's not written on a cue card but I really love Ed and I don't want you to

00:26:42.490 --> 00:26:57.270
think I'm talking behind his back if he were here tonight I'd say like to get to

00:26:57.270 --> 00:26:59.690
Alan King that young very

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:06.290
angry man. What he's got to be angry about, I don't know, he should be very grateful.

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:13.820
In the past, he's attacked the phone company, the airlines, the medical association,

00:27:14.900 --> 00:27:24.260
all the great American institutions, now tonight, me. Now, let's see, what else do I want to say

00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:29.770
here? Well, I can't leave out. I say a few words about my very dear.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:38.330
ex-friend George Burns this man really and truly he admitted it tonight didn't he says some of the

00:27:38.330 --> 00:27:48.780
stupidest things and he expects me to laugh and I do but there's a reason for it you see after

00:27:48.780 --> 00:27:56.400
knowing each other for over 50 years not 40 50 years we finally have something in common we are

00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:57.440
both senile

00:28:07.388 --> 00:28:08.388
And now...

00:28:08.732 --> 00:28:12.112
I would like to thank everyone who made this evening possible.

00:28:12.764 --> 00:28:15.384
Remember what I said earlier that I'm...

00:28:15.708 --> 00:28:17.228
I'm a very lucky man.

00:28:18.556 --> 00:28:19.356
I want to thank.

00:28:19.740 --> 00:28:21.320
everyone for being here tonight.

00:28:23.644 --> 00:28:25.064
And as I realize,

00:28:25.532 --> 00:28:29.732
tonight as I stand up here and I look around at this lavish affair.

00:28:30.444 --> 00:28:31.364
The beautiful women.

00:28:31.692 --> 00:28:35.772
in their gowns, the men in their tuxedos, the big orchestra.

00:28:36.556 --> 00:28:39.016
When I think of all the preparation.

00:28:40.236 --> 00:28:41.716
That was necessary.

00:28:42.412 --> 00:28:46.712
To make this evening what it is, one thought keeps running me through my mind.

00:28:47.884 --> 00:28:49.964
Why couldn't they have given me the money?

00:28:52.044 --> 00:28:52.224
Thank you.
